                                "text": "Impelled anew by what Byron calls 'The various joltings of life's hackney-coach,' he proceeded to Paris, and entered upon the office; but neither his age, nor his quiet unintriguing character, was congenial with the temper of such a scene; and he retired unsuccessful, but with the grant of a pension."
